Modifications by stock_trading_helper
-------------------------------------
The upstream SKILL.md is stored verbatim. Code is not vendored wholesale:
`tools/astock_extract.py` extracts only the functions listed in
`source/stock_analysis/data_sources/_astock_manifest.json` and writes them to
`source/stock_analysis/data_sources/_astock_generated.py`.

The extractor applies exactly one mechanical modification to the extracted
source: upstream HTTP timeout literals are replaced by the module constant
`_ASTOCK_HTTP_TIMEOUT` (see the manifest's "modifications" section). This is
needed so a calendar lookup can fail fast and fall back to the local weekday
estimate instead of blocking a CLI call for up to 50 seconds. No algorithmic
logic is changed.

Sections used
-------------
* "市场前缀规则（全局通用）" — get_prefix / norm_ticker
* "V3.9.0 共用 helper"        — HTTP/JSON/number/frame helpers
* "§1.1 腾讯财经 API"          — tencent_quote (optional realtime snapshot)
* "§1.2 腾讯 K 线"             — tencent_kline (raw daily bars)
* "§1.6 新浪复权因子"          — sina_adjust_factor / apply_adjust
  (Tencent qfq is an arithmetic/dividend-subtraction convention; upstream
   explicitly recommends raw bars + §1.6 ratio factors for long backtests.
   The adapter follows that recommendation so the numbers stay compatible
   with the existing Sina cache.)
* "§12 指数与交易日历"         — trading_calendar (SZSE official calendar)

Regenerate with:
    python tools/astock_extract.py
Verify without touching the working tree:
    python tools/astock_extract.py --check
